; Plan 04's rule 1, the SMF half: a file tempura never wrote has no
; essence in it, and the document it dumps to must still be usable. The
; runner wraps the fixture in the smallest document that can hold it —
; an anchor, the core's own dump, `:conductor` naming that anchor — and
; the SKELETON states the lanes and cues the bytes actually justify.
;
; `(read)` first, so the golden says what the core made of the file.
; `(dump)` then shows the derived TIMELINE tier and nothing else: one
; bound `notes` lane for the channel that sounds, one bound `curve` for
; controller 7 (which moved three times) and one for the pitch bend
; (which moved twice) — and NOTHING for controller 10, which was set once
; and is a setting, not automation. The marker is a cue.
;
; `(build :kind mid)` writes the inline tier back through the canonical
; writer: rung 1 over a file the writer itself produced, which is plan
; 09's ladder standing on its own feet.
(read)
(dump)
(build :kind mid)
(at :tick 0)
(at :tick 184504320)
